course: dictionary
lesson: 6985
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «The little girl ran to her papa when he came home.» Here papa means father or dad, because the girl runs to him when he comes home.
explain: Some words change meaning from family to family. In some families, papa means grandfather. Check the words around it: if the story is about a grandad and his grandchildren, papa means grandad, not dad.
explain: Sometimes the word is not about people at all. In the Goldilocks story, «Papa Bear» is the big bear, the name of a character. On the radio, the word papa stands for the letter P. When you read papa, ask which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in to check.
fact: Papa means dad or father, and it is an old-fashioned or family word.
fact: In some families, papa means grandfather or grandad.
fact: On the radio, police and pilots spell the letter P as «Papa».
fact: «Papa» also means dad in French, Italian and Spanish (papá).
fact: In Ukrainian, the usual word for dad is «tato», as in «Tato means dad; some families say papa, but tato is the most Ukrainian word.»
exercise: «My papa taught me to ride a bike.» What does papa mean here? | A bear in a story | A teacher at school | The letter P | * Dad
exercise: On the radio, a pilot says «Papa» to spell a letter. Which letter is it? | * P | N | Z | A
exercise: Which is the usual Ukrainian word for dad? | Grandad | Papa | * Tato | Papas
test: In the Goldilocks story, «Papa Bear» is the big bear. What does papa mean here? | Dad | A grandfather in a family | The letter P | * A character's name in a story
test: In some families, which person might papa mean? | * A grandfather | A baby | A police officer | A pilot on the radio
exam: A word can have several meanings, so how do you choose the right one? | Skip the sentence and never come back | Guess the first meaning you think of | Use the longest meaning you can find | * Read the words around it and check your meaning fits the sentence
